{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"s\">\n  <state id=\"s\">\n    <invoke type=\"echo\"/>\n    <invoke type=\"https://stateforward.org/scxml/services/echo\" id=\"svc\"/>\n    <invoke type=\"scxml\" src=\"child.scxml\"/>\n    <transition event=\"done.invoke.svc\" target=\"f\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"f\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/invoke-service-types.scxml"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":0,"notes":0,"total":2,"warnings":2},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/invoke-service-types.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":23,"endLine":3,"startColumn":19,"startLine":3}}}],"message":{"markdown":"this `<invoke type>` is a platform-specific value, not a URI\n\n**Note:** SCXML 6.4.1 allows platform-specific invoke types; a service package binds an invoked service by an exact absolute URI (a scheme, `:`, no white space, at most 4096 bytes), so this `<invoke>` raises error.execution when it runs unless the running platform defines this type\n\n**Help:** write the service's absolute type URI exactly as its service package declares it (`service-uri`), or `scxml` for an SCXML session\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §6.4 <invoke>","text":"this `<invoke type>` is a platform-specific value, not a URI"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":136,"start":132},"category":"semantic"},"ruleId":"SCXML093"},{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/invoke-service-types.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":63,"endLine":4,"startColumn":19,"startLine":4}}}],"message":{"markdown":"no service package binds this `<invoke type>`\n\n**Note:** an invoked service runs only in the service component its host binds to the exact type URI; invocation is a runtime action, so without one this `<invoke>` raises error.execution when it runs\n\n**Help:** bind the service with its package manifest (`--service-package MANIFEST.json`), or correct the URI to one a bound package declares\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §6.4 <invoke>","text":"no service package binds this `<invoke type>`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":202,"start":158},"category":"package"},"ruleId":"SCXML094"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"an absent `type`, `scxml`, or `http://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/` (with or without the trailing slash) invokes an SCXML session; any other literal type names an invoked service. SCXML 6.4.1 allows platform-specific type values, but a service package binds an invoked service by an exact absolute URI (a scheme, `:`, no white space, at most 4096 bytes), so on a host built from this repository an `<invoke>` of a type that is not a URI raises `error.execution` when it runs. Invocation is a runtime action: the document still compiles and runs"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: write the service's absolute type URI exactly as its service package declares it (`service-uri`), or `scxml` for an SCXML session.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §6.4.1 Attribute Details\n\nRun `scxml-cli --explain SCXML093` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#invoke","id":"SCXML093","name":"SCXML093","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an `<invoke type>` is a platform-specific value, not a URI"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"an invoked service runs only in the service component its host binds to the exact type URI; the validator was given the service packages the run binds, and none declares this URI. Invocation is a runtime action (SCXML 6.4): the document compiles and runs, and this `<invoke>` raises `error.execution` when it runs unless the running host binds the type. Reported only when the validator is given its service packages (`scxml-cli validate` always is: none by default)"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: bind the service with its package manifest (`--service-package MANIFEST.json`), or correct the URI to one a bound package declares.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §6.4 <invoke>\n\nRun `scxml-cli --explain SCXML094` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#invoke","id":"SCXML094","name":"SCXML094","properties":{"category":"package"},"shortDescription":{"text":"no service package binds a literal `<invoke type>`"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}